            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski Thanks for your work!\r\n\r\n\r\n> why this is a problem and needs to be changed\r\n\r\n\r\nBecause that behaviour is different from other functions.\r\n\r\n> Do you have a specific use case where this causes issues?\r\n\r\n\r\nI'm not. But, not hard to suggest that in form like that.\r\n```vim\r\n--\" not MiniPick.is_picker_active\r\n:lua MiniPick.set_picker_items(\"items\")          --\"     throws an error\r\n:lua MiniPick.set_picker_items_from_cli(\"items\") --\" not throws an error\r\n```\r\nIf it is not a sufficient reason for a change, then I will close the PR.\r\n",
